# CrestWatch runs with NO environment variables. Clone it and run it.
#
# Every data source is free and needs no key:
#   Federal: Census geocoder · USGS EPQS (ground height) · NOAA NWPS (river
#            forecasts) · USGS Water Services and the USGS Water Data API
#            (gauge readings) · NWS alerts (api.weather.gov)
#   Not federal (address search only, after the Census misses):
#            OpenStreetMap Nominatim · Open-Meteo place search (GeoNames data)
#
# Optional. Never required. Recommended on Vercel before Jan 11, 2027,
# when the new USGS API becomes the first source and anonymous use is
# limited to "a few queries per hour".
# A free api.data.gov key raises the USGS Water Data API's rate limits.
# Without it CrestWatch calls that API without a key, exactly as before.
# When set, the key is sent only to https://api.waterdata.usgs.gov.
# Get one at https://api.waterdata.usgs.gov/signup/
# USGS_API_KEY=
